{
  "id": "ASTIS-RT-20261007-SmoothedScorePosterior",
  "state": "accepted",
  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:sphmc-smoothed-score-posterior",
    "anchor": "Section3.1 and literal unnumbered S4.Ex9 (not numbered S4.E9/(4.9)); source normalized Hessian in Section2",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex9",
    "original_text": "Literal pinned primary components of the exact mean identity; numerical/transport/main bounds excluded:\n\nANCHOR S1.E1\n<table id=\"S1.E1\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S1.E1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\qquad\\kappa\\coloneqq\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V(x)\\preceq\\beta I\\,,\\qquad x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}\\,,\\qquad\\kappa\\coloneqq\\frac{\\beta}{\\alpha}\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(1.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S1.p1.1\n<p id=\"S1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">We study the problem of sampling from a target probability density <math id=\"S1.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\pi\\propto\\exp(-V)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi\\propto\\exp(-V)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id=\"S1.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{R}^{d}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where\n<math id=\"S1.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies, for <math id=\"S1.p1.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0&lt;\\alpha\\leqslant\\beta\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0&lt;\\alpha\\leqslant\\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>\nANCHOR S2.E1\n<table id=\"S2.E1\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S2.E1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)\\coloneqq\\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}{\\Bigl\\{V(x)+\\frac{\\lVert x-y\\rVert^{2}}{2a}\\Bigr\\}}\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.1389em\">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace=\"0.1389em\" rspace=\"0em\">argmin</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\operatorname{prox}_{aV}(y)\\coloneqq\\operatorname*{argmin}_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{d}}{\\Bigl\\{V(x)+\\frac{\\lVert x-y\\rVert^{2}}{2a}\\Bigr\\}}\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S2.Ex1\n<table id=\"S2.Ex1\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S2.Ex1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"R_{a,y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\lVert x-y\\rVert^{2}}{2a}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{a,y}(\\mathrm{d}x)\\propto\\exp\\Bigl\\{-V(x)-\\frac{\\lVert x-y\\rVert^{2}}{2a}\\Bigr\\}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S2.p1.1\n<p id=\"S2.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Except in the generic warm start result <a href=\"#S6.Thmtheorem1\" title=\"Theorem 6.1 (Recursive warm start generator). ‣ 6.1 Main result ‣ 6 Recursive warm start generator ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Theorem</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">6.1</span></a>\nand its consequence <a href=\"#S7.Thmtheorem1\" title=\"Theorem 7.1 (Picard HMC warm starts). ‣ 7.1 Picard HMC warm starts ‣ 7 Picard HMC warm starts and the high-accuracy sampler ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">Theorem</span> <span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">7.1</span></a>, throughout the remainder of the paper\n<math id=\"S2.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V\\in C^{2}(\\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> and (<a href=\"#S1.E1\" title=\"Equation 1.1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">1.1</span></a>) holds pointwise.\nFor most of the paper, we normalize <math id=\"S2.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\beta=1\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id=\"S2.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\kappa^{-1}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V\\preceq I\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa^{-1}I\\preceq\\nabla^{2}V\\preceq I</annotation></semantics></math>; this can be achieved by rescaling.</p>\nANCHOR S2.p3.1\n<p id=\"S2.p3.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">The sampling analogue of the proximal operator is the restricted Gaussian oracle (RGO), which is the distribution</p>\nANCHOR S3.E1\n<table id=\"S3.E1\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S3.E1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)=\\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\nabla V(X)\\bigm|X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G=y\\bigr]\\,,\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.200em\" minsize=\"1.200em\">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence=\"false\" maxsize=\"1.200em\" minsize=\"1.200em\" rspace=\"0.167em\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.200em\" minsize=\"1.200em\" rspace=\"0.170em\">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)=\\mathbb{E}\\bigl[\\nabla V(X)\\bigm|X+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G=y\\bigr]\\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(3.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S3.E2\n<table id=\"S3.E2\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S3.E2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)\\coloneqq\\nabla V\\bigl(\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G\\bigr)\\,,\\qquad G\\sim\\mathsf{N}(0,I)\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.200em\" minsize=\"1.200em\">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize=\"1.200em\" minsize=\"1.200em\" rspace=\"0.170em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)\\coloneqq\\nabla V\\bigl(\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G\\bigr)\\,,\\qquad G\\sim\\mathsf{N}(0,I)\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td>\n<td rowspan=\"1\" class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right\">(3.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S3.Ex1\n<table id=\"S3.Ex1\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S3.Ex1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\pi_{\\eta}\\coloneqq\\pi*\\mathsf{N}(0,\\eta I)\\,,\\qquad\\Pi_{\\eta}\\coloneqq\\pi_{\\eta}\\otimes\\mathsf{N}(0,I)\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace=\"0.222em\" rspace=\"0.222em\">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.170em\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0.222em\" rspace=\"0.222em\">⊗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_{\\eta}\\coloneqq\\pi*\\mathsf{N}(0,\\eta I)\\,,\\qquad\\Pi_{\\eta}\\coloneqq\\pi_{\\eta}\\otimes\\mathsf{N}(0,I)\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S3.SS1.p1.1\n<p id=\"S3.SS1.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">For a smoothing variance\n<math id=\"S3.SS1.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\eta&gt;0\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>\nANCHOR S3.SS1.p2.1\n<p id=\"S3.SS1.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">The smoothed\npotential <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"V_{\\eta}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_{\\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined by\n<math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"e^{-V_{\\eta}}\\coloneqq e^{-V}*\\mathsf{N}(0,\\eta I)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace=\"0.222em\" rspace=\"0.222em\">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">e^{-V_{\\eta}}\\coloneqq e^{-V}*\\mathsf{N}(0,\\eta I)</annotation></semantics></math>, is given by</p>\nANCHOR S3.SS1.p2.2\n<p id=\"S3.SS1.p2.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">where <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"G\\sim\\mathsf{N}(0,I)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G\\sim\\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"X\\sim\\pi\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">X\\sim\\pi</annotation></semantics></math> are independent.\nThe smoothed potential admits quantitative higher-order derivative bounds, allowing us to apply higher-order integrators.\nThe catch is that (<a href=\"#S3.E1\" title=\"Equation 3.1 ‣ 3.1 The smoothing trick ‣ 3 Technical overview ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">3.1</span></a>) is given as a conditional expectation, and is therefore not explicitly computable.\nWrite <math id=\"S3.SS1.p2.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"g_{\\eta}\\coloneqq\\nabla V_{\\eta}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_{\\eta}\\coloneqq\\nabla V_{\\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\nANCHOR S3.SS1.p3.2\n<p id=\"S3.SS1.p3.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">The intuition is that\n<math id=\"S3.SS1.p3.m2\" class=\"ltx_math_unparsed\" alttext=\"\\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)=\\int\\nabla V\\,\\mathrm{d}R_{\\eta,y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace=\"0.111em\">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)=\\int\\nabla V\\,\\mathrm{d}R_{\\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and\n<math id=\"S3.SS1.p3.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\law(\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G)\\approx R_{\\eta,y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\law(\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)+\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,G)\\approx R_{\\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that\n<math id=\"S3.SS1.p3.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)</annotation></semantics></math> is almost an unbiased estimator of\n<math id=\"S3.SS1.p3.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla V_{\\eta}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\nANCHOR S4.Ex3\n<table id=\"S4.Ex3\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.Ex3.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"x_{y}^{+}\\coloneqq\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x_{y}^{+}\\coloneqq\\operatorname{prox}_{\\eta V}(y)\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S4.Ex8\n<table id=\"S4.Ex8\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.Ex8.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\rho_{y}(u)\\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\\sqrt{\\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\langle\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\\rangle\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace=\"0.170em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\rho_{y}(u)\\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\\sqrt{\\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\\sqrt{\\eta}\\,\\langle\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\\rangle\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S4.Ex9\n<table id=\"S4.Ex9\" class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table\">\n\n<tbody><tr class=\"ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline\">\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft\"></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center\"><math id=\"S4.Ex9.m1\" class=\"ltx_math_unparsed\" alttext=\"g_{\\eta}(y)=\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\\eta^{-1/2}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathsf{r}_{y}}\\nabla\\rho_{y}(U)\\,,\\qquad\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)=\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\\eta^{-1/2}\\,\\nabla\\rho_{y}(G)\\,.\" display=\"block\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace=\"0.167em\" rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace=\"0.170em\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace=\"2.167em\">,</mo><msub><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace=\"0.167em\" rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace=\"0.170em\">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">g_{\\eta}(y)=\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\\eta^{-1/2}\\,\\mathbb{E}_{\\mathsf{r}_{y}}\\nabla\\rho_{y}(U)\\,,\\qquad\\widehat{g}_{\\eta}(y;G)=\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\\eta^{-1/2}\\,\\nabla\\rho_{y}(G)\\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td class=\"ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright\"></td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\nANCHOR S4.SS1.p4.1\n<p id=\"S4.SS1.p4.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S4.SS1.p4.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Proximal optimality gives\n<math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\\eta\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>\nANCHOR S4.SS1.p4.2\n<p id=\"S4.SS1.p4.2\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S4.SS1.p4.2.1\" class=\"ltx_text\">Then <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"0\\preceq\\nabla^{2}\\rho_{y}\\preceq\\eta I\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace=\"0.167em\">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0\\preceq\\nabla^{2}\\rho_{y}\\preceq\\eta I</annotation></semantics></math>, and under <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"R_{\\eta,y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">R_{\\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>,\n<math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"(X-x_{y}^{+})/\\sqrt{\\eta}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(X-x_{y}^{+})/\\sqrt{\\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> has density\nproportional to <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m5\" class=\"ltx_math_unparsed\" alttext=\"u\\mapsto e^{-\\lVert u\\rVert^{2}/2-\\rho_{y}(u)}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">↦</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">u\\mapsto e^{-\\lVert u\\rVert^{2}/2-\\rho_{y}(u)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Call this law <math id=\"S4.SS1.p4.m6\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathsf{r}_{y}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.\nWe have</span></p>\nANCHOR S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1\n<p id=\"S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\"><span id=\"S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_font_italic\">Write</span></p>",
    "text_sha256": "36c5010dd567619a9b99385aeb05ea38bb63071365b18c18b43401dc7da64c0d"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.SmoothedScorePosterior.smoothed_score_posterior",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/SmoothedScorePosterior.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {κ η : ℝ} (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2) (hη : 0 < η) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let C := ((Real.sqrt (2*Real.pi*η))⁻¹)^Module.finrank ℝ E\n    let A := fun y : E => C*∫ x, Real.exp (-V x-‖y-x‖^2/(2*η)) ∂(volume : Measure E)\n    let Vη := fun y : E => -Real.log (A y)\n    let R := fun y : E => μ.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y‖^2/(2*η))\n    IsProbabilityMeasure μ ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 Vη ∧\n      (∀ y, IsProbabilityMeasure (R y) ∧ MemLp id 2 (R y) ∧\n        Integrable (gradient V) (R y) ∧\n        gradient Vη y = ∫ x, gradient V x ∂(R y)) ∧\n      ∃ p : E → E, Measurable p ∧ (∀ y, p y+η • gradient V (p y)=y) ∧\n        let rho := fun y u => V (p y+Real.sqrt η • u)-V (p y)-\n          Real.sqrt η*inner ℝ (gradient V (p y)) u\n        let r := fun y => (R y).map (fun x => (Real.sqrt η)⁻¹ • (x-p y))\n        ∀ y, r y=(volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u => -(‖u‖^2/2+rho y u)) ∧\n          IsProbabilityMeasure (r y) ∧ MemLp (gradient (rho y)) 2 (r y) ∧\n          gradient Vη y=gradient V (p y)+(Real.sqrt η)⁻¹ • (∫ u, gradient (rho y) u ∂(r y)) ∧\n          ∀ z, gradient V (p y+Real.sqrt η • z)=\n            gradient V (p y)+(Real.sqrt η)⁻¹ • gradient (rho y) z",
    "statement_sha256": "de01bb158b9b17979738c28eafb1d98980bd51b0facf61c52d443f837e1a5a74",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "Measure.tilted is the actual normalized exponential tilt against its indicated base. Measure.map is the actual measurable pushforward. All displayed integrals are Bochner integrals.",
      "volume is the canonical finite real Hilbert Haar/Lebesgue measure with its Borel structure. Dimension zero is included. gradient is the real Riesz representative of the Frechet derivative.",
      "The potential defined by minus log A uses the literal unnormalized volume convolution with the displayed Gaussian prefactor. It is not defined by an assumed gradient identity.",
      "The second tilt retains the original potential and the quadratic denominator exactly. Its affine pushforward uses the same produced measurable stationary point p and square-root scale. No selector, normalizer, moment or mean identity is supplied.",
      "MemLp at exponent two means actual square-integrability. Integrable means actual Bochner first integrability. The positive real eta has no upper cap."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "runs/20261007-companion-priority/smoothed-score-posterior/focused.tests.4.log PASS3751, standard3 only; local compilation only."
  },
